OL,3,CProgramme listings for SUN 5 APR
OL,4,G1800FChoral Evensong
OL,5,     GFrom the Chapel of King's
OL,6,     GCollege, Cambridge on Easter Day,
OL,7,     Gwith music by Wood and Elgar.
OL,8,G1900FSunday Feature: February House
OL,9,     GFor a year during World War II,
OL,10,     Gan unremarkable residence in
OL,11,     GBrooklyn Heights, New York City,
OL,12,     Gbecame an epicentre of Western
OL,13,     Gmusic and literature.
OL,14,G1945FWords and Music
OL,15,     GReadings from Natalie Simpson and
OL,16,     GRay Fearon on the transcendent
OL,17,     Gand numinous, from Shakespeare
OL,18,     Gand Donne to Wordsworth and
OL,19,     GLarkin. Music from Beethoven to
OL,20,     GBruckner.
